  "topics": [
    {
      "number": 1,
      "title": "Finding A⁻¹ by Row Reduction",
      "abbr": "ECE",
      "subtopics": [
        {
          "number": "1.1",
          "title": "Finding A⁻¹ by Row Reduction",
          "abbr": "ECE",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<p>Augment A with the identity matrix I to form [A | I]. Then apply row operations until the left side becomes I. Whatever appears on the right side at that point is A⁻¹. The idea: every operation you do to A, you also do to I, and by the time A is reduced to I, those operations have built up A⁻¹ on the right.</p>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<strong>Row Reduction Method for Inverse</strong>"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "<div>[A | I] → row operations → [I | A⁻¹] Then use A⁻¹ to solve AX = B: X = A⁻¹ · B</div>"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Only works if det(A) ≠ 0. If A reduces to something other than I on the left, it is singular and has no inverse."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<span>2019/2020 Q4f — Solve 2x+5y=6, 3x+4y=8 using inverse matrix method</span>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<strong>01</strong>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<strong>Write the system as AX = B</strong>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<pre>A = [ 2 5 ] X = [ x ] B = [ 6 ] [ 3 4 ] [ y ] [ 8 ] AX = B becomes [ 2 5 ][ x ] = [ 6 ] [ 3 4 ][ y ] [ 8 ]</pre>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<strong>02</strong>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<strong>Set up augmented matrix [A | I]</strong>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<pre>[ 2 5 | 1 0 ] [ 3 4 | 0 1 ]</pre>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<strong>03</strong>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<strong>Make pivot (1,1) = 1: R₁' = R₁ ÷ 2</strong>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<pre>[ 1 5/2 | 1/2 0 ] [ 3 4 | 0 1 ]</pre>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<strong>04</strong>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<strong>Clear column 1: R₂' = R₂ − 3·R₁'</strong>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<pre>R₂': [3-3, 4-3(5/2), 0-3(1/2), 1-0] = [0, 4-15/2, -3/2, 1] = [0, -7/2, -3/2, 1] [ 1 5/2 | 1/2 0 ] [ 0 -7/2 | -3/2 1 ]</pre>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<strong>05</strong>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<strong>Make pivot (2,2) = 1: R₂'' = R₂' × (−2/7)</strong>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<pre>R₂'' = R₂' × (-2/7): [0, (-7/2)(-2/7), (-3/2)(-2/7), (1)(-2/7)] = [0, 1, 3/7, -2/7] [ 1 5/2 | 1/2 0 ] [ 0 1 | 3/7 -2/7]</pre>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<strong>06</strong>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<strong>Clear column 2 above: R₁'' = R₁' − (5/2)·R₂''</strong>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<pre>R₁'': [1-0, 5/2-(5/2)(1), 1/2-(5/2)(3/7), 0-(5/2)(-2/7)] = [1, 0, 1/2-15/14, 5/7] = [1, 0, 7/14-15/14, 5/7] = [1, 0, -8/14, 5/7] = [1, 0, -4/7, 5/7] [ 1 0 | -4/7 5/7 ] [ 0 1 | 3/7 -2/7 ] A⁻¹ = [ -4/7 5/7 ] [ 3/7 -2/7 ]</pre>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<strong>07</strong>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<strong>Solve X = A⁻¹ · B</strong>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<pre>X = A⁻¹ · B = [ -4/7 5/7 ] × [ 6 ] [ 3/7 -2/7 ] [ 8 ] x = (-4/7)(6) + (5/7)(8) = -24/7 + 40/7 = 16/7 y = (3/7)(6) + (-2/7)(8) = 18/7 - 16/7 = 2/7</pre>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<div>x = 16/7, y = 2/7</div>"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "<strong>Exam focus:</strong>"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Solve 2x+5y=6, 3x+4y=8 in form AX=B using inverse matrix method. (2019/2020 Q4f, 5 marks)",
                "Determine C⁻¹ for C = [[10,15,0],[2,4,0],[3,6,6]] given p(λ) = λ³ − 20λ² + 94λ − 60. (2019/2020 Q3d, 5 marks — use Cayley-Hamilton)",
                "Find A⁻¹ using row reduction for a 2×2 or 3×3 matrix, then verify AA⁻¹ = I."
              ]
            }
          ],
